10
01:02:46,666 --> 01:02:52,666
Hope and Glory is a 1987 comedy-drama war film written, produced, and directed by John
Boorman based on his own experiences growing up in London during World War II.

11
01:09:03,333 --> 01:09:09,333
It was distributed by Columbia Pictures.

12
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
The title is derived from the patriotic British song "Land of Hope and Glory".

13
01:21:36,666 --> 01:21:42,666
The film tells the story of the Rohan family and their experiences, as seen
through the eyes of the son, Billy (Sebastian Rice-Edwards).

14
01:27:53,333 --> 01:27:59,333
A critical and commercial success, the film won the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy and received five
Academy Award nominations, including Best Picture, Best Director, and Best Original Screenplay (all for Boorman).

15
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:16,000
It also received 13 BAFTA Award nominations, winning for Best
Actress in a Supporting Role (Susan Wooldridge).

16
01:40:26,666 --> 01:40:32,666
The film explores themes of london, england, wartime, based on
true story, semi autobiographical, home front.

17
01:46:43,333 --> 01:46:49,333
The tone is emotional.
